INT. HOUSEBOAT GALLEY - MORNING

A narrow kitchen on a canal boat. Copper pans swing gently with the water. Rain taps the porthole.

ZOFIA NOWAK (70s, tiny, apron over a quilted vest) rolls dough on a board nailed to the counter. Her son WALEED (40s, tired eyes, a dress shirt with one sleeve rolled) stands at the stove, stirring a pot he is not hungry for.

At the table, PRIYA (16, headphones around her neck) peels an orange in one unbroken spiral. Beside her, KOFI (8, pajamas, a plastic dinosaur in each fist) crashes them together.

A landline phone hangs on the bulkhead. It rings.

                    WALEED
          Don't.

                    ZOFIA
          I wasn't.

It rings again. Priya peels. Kofi roars his dinosaurs into the sugar bowl.

                    ZOFIA (CONT'D)
          Somebody should.

                    WALEED
          It's the lawyer. Or the marina.

                    ZOFIA
          Or it's Marguerite.

Waleed stops stirring. The phone rings a fourth time. Priya sets down the orange.

                    WALEED
          Priya, would you --

                    PRIYA
          Why me?

                    WALEED
          Because you're closest.

                    PRIYA
          I'm not closest. Gran is closest.

                    ZOFIA
          My hands are in flour.

Priya gets up, lifts the receiver. Holds it a few inches from her ear.

                    PRIYA
          Hello?

                    MARGUERITE (V.O.)
                (phone)
          Is your father there?

                    PRIYA
          He's... stirring.

                    MARGUERITE (V.O.)
                (phone)
          Tell him I'm at the lock. I'll be there in twenty minutes.

Priya looks at her father. He looks at the soup. Zofia presses the dough flat with both thumbs, harder than the recipe needs.

                    PRIYA
          She says twenty minutes.

                    WALEED
          Tell her we're out.

                    ZOFIA
          Tell her we have enough bread.

                    WALEED
          Mama.

                    ZOFIA
          Waleed.

                    WALEED
          Don't --

                    ZOFIA
          Don't what?

                    WALEED
          (together)
          Don't start.

                    ZOFIA
          (together)
          I'm not starting.

                    PRIYA
          (into the phone)
          Come. It's... fine.

She hangs up. Silence. Kofi's dinosaurs go quiet. The boat rocks. A drop falls from the porthole frame onto the sill.

Zofia takes down a fourth bowl from the shelf. Then a fifth. Sets them on the table without comment.

Waleed puts the spoon down. Rolls the other sleeve to match the first. Kofi slides a dinosaur across the table until it stops beside the fifth bowl.
